WEBVTT

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:02.490
Section sixteen.

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:06.430
Stronger retrieval and contextual retrieval.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:10.190
The purpose is to investigate specific weaknesses without

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:13.210
mistaking architectural complexity for improvement.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:17.410
Everything in the research lane is a proposal or

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:18.250
external reference,

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.690
not a current product capability.

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:30.770
First

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:32.590
preserve complete sentences,

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:35.450
decisive passages, and contradiction.

00:00:36.778 --> 00:00:40.258
Align evidence validation with exactly what was transmitted.

00:00:41.966 --> 00:00:45.026
Compare candidate-conditioned passage selection with today's

00:00:45.026 --> 00:00:47.546
simple packing at the same token ceiling.

00:00:49.134 --> 00:00:51.134
Sparse experiments can vary term frequency,

00:00:51.794 --> 00:00:52.374
field weights,

00:00:53.194 --> 00:00:53.594
alias order,

00:00:54.274 --> 00:00:55.654
boosts, and smaller caps.

00:00:56.862 --> 00:01:00.082
These tests ask which error is fixed, rather than

00:01:00.082 --> 00:01:01.782
assuming the next layer must be better.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:11.340
A public-only bi-encoder trial could embed concept definitions and

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:13.640
repository-purpose profiles separately.

00:01:14.359 --> 00:01:18.579
A small registry can use exact local similarity before

00:01:18.579 --> 00:01:20.219
an approximate-neighbor service.

00:01:21.617 --> 00:01:23.837
Cache by content and encoder version;

00:01:24.677 --> 00:01:26.777
preserve identity and access metadata.

00:01:27.696 --> 00:01:30.416
If dense search recovers real lexical misses,

00:01:31.336 --> 00:01:34.556
compare sparse and dense unions with reciprocal-rank fusion.

00:01:35.554 --> 00:01:39.194
A reranker adds cost and cannot recover a candidate

00:01:39.194 --> 00:01:40.514
absent from that union.

00:01:42.013 --> 00:01:44.813
Private embeddings are derived content and need separate

00:01:44.813 --> 00:01:45.293
permission.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.900
Now, contextual retrieval.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.180
Its purpose is to make an indexed chunk meaningful

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:57.840
beyond its isolated words.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:02.600
Anthropic's approach adds document-conditioned context before

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:08.400
indexing chunks with embeddings and BM25, with optional reranking.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:12.040
Our deterministic metadata and purpose excerpts are not that

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:12.600
mechanism.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:17.300
A trial could compare cheap metadata prefixes with generated

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:17.960
context,

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:19.880
accounting for indexing,

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:20.780
refresh,

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:23.300
privacy, and downstream support.

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:27.980
External published results do not become measured GitHub Manager

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:31.040
improvements merely by showing the reference diagram.

00:02:36.108 --> 00:02:40.371
A future controller could allow one extra source-linked evidence

00:02:40.371 --> 00:02:43.311
pass after an insufficient-context result,

00:02:44.011 --> 00:02:47.211
under a reviewed budget, then abstain.

00:02:48.651 --> 00:02:51.991
Adaptive RAG, Self-RAG, and corrective RAG are research

00:02:51.991 --> 00:02:52.471
references,

00:02:53.231 --> 00:02:54.731
not adopted implementations.

00:02:55.691 --> 00:02:59.071
Agentic retrieval would additionally need tool permissions and

00:02:59.071 --> 00:03:00.211
trajectory evaluation.

00:03:01.271 --> 00:03:05.451
Domain relationships alone do not create GraphRAG.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:08.771
Application memory does not make the model remember conversations.
